From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joostlek <joostlek@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:21:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix verify_event_loop_thread when HomeAssistant is patched

verify_event_loop_thread resolves where to find hass on the first call
of each decorated function. It checks isinstance(obj, HomeAssistant)
and reads HomeAssistant from the module globals at call time.

The stop_hass test fixture and tests/test_bootstrap.py patch
homeassistant.core.HomeAssistant with a function or a mock. If the first
call happens while the patch is active, isinstance raises TypeError.
The failure depends on test order.

Keep an unpatched module-level reference to the class and use it in the
isinstance check. This keeps the current resolution order and behavior
for mocks. It also fixes the problem for every test that patches the
class, not only the two known sites.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Without this, tests/test_bootstrap.py fails with 20 errors when it is
run alone (also with an unpatched 2026.11.0 and on dev), and in about
half of the ptest runs, depending on which tests run first on a worker.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/home-assistant/core/pull/188003]
The PR was approved, then closed by its author without being merged.

---
 homeassistant/core.py | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/homeassistant/core.py b/homeassistant/core.py
index c420406a..4f946e71 100644
--- a/homeassistant/core.py
+++ b/homeassistant/core.py
@@ -246,7 +246,7 @@ def verify_event_loop_thread[**_P, _R](
 
         def resolve_get_hass(obj: Any) -> HomeAssistant:
             nonlocal get_hass
-            if isinstance(obj, HomeAssistant):
+            if isinstance(obj, _HomeAssistant):
                 get_hass = _get_hass_identity
             elif hasattr(obj, "hass"):
                 get_hass = _get_hass_public
@@ -1341,6 +1341,11 @@ class HomeAssistant:
             _LOGGER.warning("Shutdown stage '%s': still running: %s", stage, task)
 
 
+# Tests patch homeassistant.core.HomeAssistant with a function.
+# verify_event_loop_thread uses this reference so isinstance keeps working.
+_HomeAssistant = HomeAssistant
+
+
 class Context:
     """The context that triggered something."""
 
